 """Decide which files in a project tree are ignored by its .gitignore files.
 
-This currently delegates to git: it copies the tree into a scratch repository
-and asks `git ls-files` which untracked files are ignored.
+This is a pure-Python reimplementation of what
+`git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard` reports for a fresh
+repository whose only exclude sources are the .gitignore files in the tree
+(no global excludes file, no .git/info/exclude, core.ignorecase=false).
+
+It mirrors git's own code closely (dir.c for reading and applying patterns,
+wildmatch.c for glob matching) so that unusual patterns behave the same way.
+Everything works on bytes, as git does: `?` and `[...]` match single bytes.
